sched/fair: cgroup deadline servers prototype (Task 3 option B)

Prototype: when kernel.sched_cgroup_dl_servers=1 (default 0), admit a
per-CPU deadline server for bandwidth-root cgroups — groups that have
cpu.max set and no ancestor below root also has quota. That covers
survey "depth-1 under root with cpu.max" and deeper first-capped leaves
(the Task 3 harness throttle groups).

When enabled:
- Server pick starts at that group's cfs_rq (pick_task_fair_from), not
  always at the root.
- CFS bandwidth period refill / throttling stay authoritative; we do
  NOT bypass distribute_cfs_runtime. The DL server is an additional
  fair_server-style pick path (50ms/1000ms params) for enqueue cost.
- Hierarchical cpu.weight among opted-in siblings is NOT rebuilt —
  weight sharing may be wrong/ignored on the DL pick path. This is a
  prototype for enqueue/bandwidth-timer cost, not a shipping cgroup
  redesign.

Feature off (default) => identical to stock (static key; no servers
allocated). Enable before creating capped cgroups:
  sudo sysctl -w kernel.sched_cgroup_dl_servers=1

LOCALVERSION=-t3 for the measured image.

